    "ECX_boundary": "The prior initializer may clobber ECX/EDX and flags. The PUSH and CALL preserve their actually supplied values, but this packet does not determine them.",
    "PUSH_to_CALL_entry": "If the accepted prior PUSH completes with incoming ESP=S, then it leaves ESP=S-4 and [SS:S-4]=CD9410. If this CALL then transfers normally, target-entry ESP=S-8, [SS:S-8]=CC8D44, and [SS:target-entry ESP+4]=CD9410.",
    "current_call_snapshot": "Fresh epoch98 exact five-byte CALL and per-byte gates.",
    "initializer_condition": "If S is also the prefix-entry stack value and the accepted 436230 call actually returns normally under its separate plain-RET/no-stacked-argument/receiver-return ABI, EAX=E1768C before the PUSH and remains E1768C on this CALL target entry. This is a conditional composition, not an observed invocation.",
    "no_return_cleanup_assumption": "No cdecl/stdcall/signature, target normal return, EAX status, stack cleanup or registration success is inferred. The stored _atexit label and no_return=false flag do not supply those contracts.",
    "prior_PUSH_snapshot": "Accepted epoch95 CC8D3A..3E PUSH imm32 CD9410; inherited five bytes, not refreshed.",
    "prior_initializer_prefix_snapshot": "Accepted epoch92 CC8D30..39 plus CE2754 and separately accepted 436230 normal-return ABI; inherited ten code/four data bytes, no callee refresh.",
    "stack_word_use_unknown": "The CD9410 word is physically at target-entry ESP+4 under those conditions. Whether/how the target uses it, whether it is a formal parameter or callback, and any ownership/lifetime contract remain unproved."
